       39  '''Glodeni District''' ({{IPAc-ro|lang|pron|G|l|o|'|d|e|ni}}) is a [[Administrative divisions of Moldova|district]] ({{Langx|ro|[[raion]]}}) in northwestern [[Moldova]], with its administrative center at [[Glodeni]]. As of the [[2024 Moldovan census]], its population was 35,829. The district consist
       40  ==History==
       41  The oldest area in the district is the [[Cobani]], which dates back to June 3, 1374 {{Cite web |last=invitat |first=Autor |date=2011-12-26 |title=The Oldest Locality in Moldova (VIDEO) |url=https://www.moldova.org/en/the-oldest-locality-in-moldova-video-227428-eng/ |access-date=2026-08-23 |website=M
       42  Since the 17th and 18th centuries, the region has been fueled by wars with the [[Polish–Lithuanian Commonwealth]] and the [[Ottoman Empire|Ottoman]] and [[Russian Empire]]s. In 1812, the region was occupied by the [[Russian Empire]]; with the local population of [[Moldovans]] and [[Ukrainians]], [[R
       43  ==Geography==
       44  Glodeni District is bordered by [[Riscani District]] on the north, [[Bălţi|Balti Municipality]] on the east, [[Falesti District]] on the south and [[Romania]] on the west. The district is a hilly plain, fragmented by valleys which are higher in the west with a slight incline to their merge with the 
       45  ===Climate===
       46  The annual average temperature is {{convert|8.5|C|F}} degrees. In January, the average temperature is {{convert|-4.5|C|F}} degrees and {{convert|20.5|C|F}} degrees in July. Annual rainfall is {{convert|480|-|560|mm|in}}. In rainy years up to {{convert|750|mm|in}} is possible, while in dry years it c
       47  ===Fauna===
       48  The district has fauna typical of Central Europe, including fox, [[weasel]], [[marten]], [[deer]], [[woodpecker]], [[European turtle dove|turtle dove]] and [[pheasant]] in forests and [[boar]], [[ondatra]], [[otter]], [[duck]], [[Lynx|wild cat]], [[egret]] near the Prut. [[Gopher (animal)|gopher]], 
       49  ===Flora===
       50  Forests occupy 8.5 percent of the district, and consist of [[oak]], [[acacia]], [[Populus|poplar]], [[Ash (Fraxinus)|ash]], [[maple]], [[elm]] and [[hazel]]. Undergrowth includes [[blackthorn]] and [[blackberry]]. [[Steppe]] and [[forest steppe]] vegetation includes grasses, [[knotweed]], [[clover]]
       51  === Pădurea Domnească===
       52  {{See also|Pădurea Domnească}}
       54  The Pădurea Domnească nature reserve is located in the mid-Prut Valley area, extending {{convert|40|km}} between [[Criva, Briceni|Criva]] and [[Pruteni]]. A forest under state protection since 1993, it is one of the most valuable meadows and old [[floodplain]] forests in Europe. The reserve covers a
       55  ===Rivers===
       56  The Prut borders Romania. Smaller rivers include the [[Camenca (Prut)|Camenca]], Căldăruşa and the Glodeni (in the Prut basin) and Copăceanca (in the [[Răut River]] basin). The district contains {{convert|1900|ha|acre}} of lakes and [[ponds]], which are popular summer retreats for tourists and local
       57  ==Demographics==
       58  According to the [[2024 Moldovan census|2024 census]], 35,829 inhabitants lived in Glodeni District, a decrease compared to the previous census in 2014, when 51,306 inhabitants were registered. {{cite web|url=https://statistica.gov.md/ro/rezultatele-finale-ale-recensamantului-populatiei-si-locuintel
